<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2589" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ănhēlātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		anhelo (post-Aug. for the earlier anhelitus), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a difficulty of
				breathing</i>, <i>panting</i>, <i>puffing.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">piscium aestivo calore,</span>”
				<i>the panting of fish</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					9, 7, 6, § 18</span></i>
			.—As a disease = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἆσθμα</span>, <i>asthma</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 23, 1,
				24, § 47</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in iis (gemmis) caelestis arcūs
					anhelatio,</span>”
				<i>breathing</i>, <i>play of</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					37, 6, 23, § 89</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
